## 6. MEMORY MANAGEMENT STRATEGY

### 6.1 Object Pooling Requirements
- **Projectiles:** Pool of 50 bullets (max simultaneous)
- **Particles:** Hard cap of 500 via ParticleSystem
- **Power-ups:** Pool of 3 power-up instances
- **Floating text:** Pool of 20 score texts

### 6.2 Explicit Disposal Protocol
```typescript
class MemoryManager {
    private resources: WeakSet<ThreeJSResource> = new WeakSet();

    track(resource: ThreeJSResource): void {
        this.resources.add(resource);
    }

    disposeGame(): void {
        this.resources.forEach(resource => {
            if (resource.dispose) resource.dispose();
        });
        this.resources.clear();
    }
}
```

### 6.3 Leak Prevention Checklist
- [ ] All Geometries disposed on pool return or game end
- [ ] All Materials disposed when enemy types change
- [ ] All Textures disposed after canvas texture generation
- [ ] All Event listeners removed on cleanup
- [ ] All Three.js objects removed from scene before disposal

---

## 7. PERFORMANCE TARGETS

### 7.1 Frame Rate Budget
- **Target:** 60 FPS sustained
- **Budget per frame:** 16.67ms
- **VFX allocation:** 
  - Particle updates: 2ms max
  - Collision detection: 3ms max (AABB is O(n²) but n ≤ 60 enemies + bullets)
  - Post-processing: 5ms max (UnrealBloomPass optimized)

### 7.2 Memory Budget
- **Total texture memory:** < 10MB (procedural textures are small)
- **Particle system:** ~2MB (500 particles × 4KB each)
- **Scene graph:** < 5MB (instanced meshes for stars, efficient geometry reuse)

---

## 8. EDGE CASES & ERROR HANDLING

### 8.1 Input Edge Cases
- **Gamepad disconnect:** Fallback to keyboard input seamlessly
- **Rapid fire spam:** Cooldown timer prevents bullet spam abuse
- **Boundary violation:** Clamp player position, bounce off walls

### 8.2 Collision Edge Cases
- **Bullet passing through:** Sub-stepping at high velocities (fixed timestep)
- **Simultaneous multi-hit:** Process one hit per frame to prevent score exploits
- **Shield penetration:** Shield absorbs first shot, then breaks permanently

### 8.3 Performance Edge Cases
- **Low-end devices:** Fallback bloom strength to 0.8, reduce particle count to 250
- **Memory pressure:** Auto-pool cleanup if heap exceeds 100MB
- **Browser tab inactive:** Pause game loop to save battery

---

## 9. DEFINITION OF DONE VERIFICATION

### 9.1 Playability Checklist
- [ ] Game launches in browser without errors
- [ ] Player can move left/right with keyboard and gamepad
- [ ] Player can shoot projectiles upward
- [ ] Enemies move, shift down at edges, and fire back
- [ ] Collision detection works for bullets hitting enemies/player
- [ ] Score updates correctly on enemy kills
- [ ] Lives system functions (3 lives, respawn mechanic)
- [ ] Win condition triggers when all enemies destroyed
- [ ] Loss condition triggers when player dies 3 times or enemies reach bottom
- [ ] All VFX systems active and visible (shake, particles, trails, etc.)

### 9.2 Performance Verification
- [ ] Frame rate stays above 50 FPS on target hardware
- [ ] No memory leaks after 10+ minute play session
- [ ] Object pooling prevents GC spikes during gameplay
- [ ] Post-processing does not cause frame drops

---

